# Meraxes (DRAGONS) AGN X-ray luminosity function after obscuration, z = 6.088 (snapshot 107).
# A MODEL line, not an observation: Type data_sim, drawn as a line with a band like Qin2017_Tiamat in QLF_UV.
#
# Quantity: the model's OBSERVED rest-frame 2-10 keV luminosity function. Each AGN is binned at its intrinsic
#     hard X-ray luminosity multiplied by the 2-10 keV transmission of the column density N_H drawn for it
#     (Ueda et al. 2014 N_H distribution, log N_H = 20-26, Compton-thick AGN included). It is NOT absorption
#     corrected, so compare it with observed luminosities, not with absorption-corrected ones.
# phi = dPhi/dlogLX in Mpc^-3 dex^-1 and LX in erg s^-1. The bins are 0.2 dex wide and tabulated at the bin centre.
# Every AGN is weighted by its duty cycle. The band is +-1 sigma of the Bernoulli variance of those weights,
#     sqrt(sum w(1-w)) / (V dlogLX), as saved by Meraxes. It reflects only which AGN are 'on'. It does NOT include
#     Poisson noise in the number of AGN in the box or cosmic variance, so it is narrower than 1/sqrt(N) by a factor
#     of 0.3-1 (the brighter the bin, the narrower, because bright AGN are nearly always on).
# Only bins that are expected to hold at least 10 active AGN are listed (phi V dlogLX >= 10); beyond that the
#     box is too small to constrain the model (one AGN per bin would be log phi = -6.78).
# Below log LX ~ 41 the line turns over because the model has no black holes below its seed mass.
#
# Model: Meraxes, Genesis L210 N4320 trees (box 210 Mpc/h, augmented trees), h = 0.6751, Omega_m = 0.3121.
#     Black hole growth rate 0.5 (not evolving with redshift), Eddington ratio 1, Shen et al. 2020
#     bolometric corrections. The Meraxes quasar model is described in Qin et al. 2017 (2017MNRAS.472.2009Q).
#     Run: the paper fiducial run X6_XAGN_Xstar_fid, snapshot 107. h in info.txt is the h of the model.
#
# logLX  phi  phi_upper  phi_lower
